</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="Ptx1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part">Appendix</h2>

<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Work</h3>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we discuss the recent success of DFM and techniques used in our work.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discrete Generative Models and Discrete Flow Matching.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While autoregressive models remain the predominant paradigm for discrete data generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Achiam et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ingraham et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, recent diffusion and flow-matching alternatives show impressive performance across many domains, including sound generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, graph generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vignac et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, and protein design <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Campbell et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
Progress in adapting these continuous-time models to discrete settings follows two strategies.
The first involves designing diffusion processes over discrete state spaces <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sohl-Dickstein et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoogeboom et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vignac et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.
The second embeds discrete data into a continuous space, where standard diffusion or flow-matching techniques then be applied <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dieleman et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Campbell et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Davis et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Most recently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Campbell et al. (2024)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gat et al., 2024</a>)</cite> introduce Discrete Flow Matching (DFM), which emerge as a powerful new paradigm for discrete generative modeling.
DFM offers significant flexibility in the design of the denoising process and the choice of the source distribution.
Consequently, there is a growing interest in exploring the efficiency and application of DFM for various generation tasks.
This interest lead to a rapid expansion of DFM-based models.
For instance, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu and Ommer, 2024</a>)</cite> validate its efficiency in the image domain.
In graph generation, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qin et al. (2024)</a></cite> introduce DeFoG, a framework that uses DFM to respect the inherent symmetries of graphs and disentangle sampling from training for more efficient optimization.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fuest et al. (2025)</a></cite> introduce MaskFlow, a unified video generation framework that leverages DFM for efficient, high-quality long video synthesis.
Similarly, in structural biology, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yi et al. (2025)</a></cite> present ADFLIP, a DFM-based model for designing protein sequences conditioned on all-atom structural contexts.
However, the success of these models are driven by empirical validation.
Despite their impressive performance and growing adoption, a rigorous theoretical understanding of DFM is lacking.
Our work fills this critical gap by providing the solid theoretical foundations for Discrete Flow Matching.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Transformer Universal Approximation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Transformers are universal approximators, possessing the capacity to model any arbitrary sequence-to-sequence function with a desired level of precision.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yun et al. (2019)</a></cite> establish universality for deep stacks of self-attention and feed-forward layers via a contextual mapping method, under the assumption that hidden representations remain sufficiently separated.
Later, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Alberti et al., 2023</a>)</cite> broaden the scope of this guarantee to encompass variants using sparse attention mechanisms.
Building on this foundation, more recent findings relax the architectural requirements. Research from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. (2024a)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kajitsuka and Sato (2023)</a></cite> demonstrate that the powerful approximation capability is not dependent on depth, showing that a single Transformer block with one self-attention layer is itself sufficient to achieve universal approximation.
In our work, we leverage this powerful result to analyze the approximation error of Transformer-based discrete flow matching models.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Supplementary Background: Transformer Block</h3>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce the transformer network structure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al., 2017</a>)</cite> and its properties.
Following the notations in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>,
We start with the definition of transformers.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Transformers</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transformer Block.</span>
Let <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of heads and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> be the hidden dimension of the multi-head attention layer.
The multi-head attention layer <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm SA}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>SA</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm SA}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> is then defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F^{\rm SA}(Z):=Z+\sum_{i=1}^{h}W_{O}^{i}(W_{V}^{i}Z)\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}((W_{K}^{i}Z)^{\top}(W_{Q}^{i}Z))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>SA</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F^{\rm SA}(Z):=Z+\sum_{i=1}^{h}W_{O}^{i}(W_{V}^{i}Z)\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}((W_{K}^{i}Z)^{\top}(W_{Q}^{i}Z)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}^{i},W_{Q}^{i},W_{V}^{i},(W_{O}^{i})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}^{i},W_{Q}^{i},W_{V}^{i},(W_{O}^{i})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> are weight matrices for all <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[h]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the column-wise softmax function.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> be the dimension of hidden of the feed-forward layer.
The feed-forward layer <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm FF}(Z):\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm FF}(Z):\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> is then defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F^{\rm FF}(Z):=Z+W_{2}\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}Z+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})+b_{2}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F^{\rm FF}(Z):=Z+W_{2}\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}Z+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})+b_{2}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1},(W_{2})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1},(W_{2})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> are weight matrices, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{r},b_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{r},b_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are bias.
Throughout this paper, we treat <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> as element-wise operation when applied to vectors or matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We define a transformer block as the composition of a self-attention layer and a feed-forward layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Transformer Block)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h,s,r\in\mathbb{Z}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h,s,r\in\mathbb{Z}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define a
transformer block <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{h,s,r}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{h,s,r}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F^{h,s,r}:=F^{\rm FF}\circ F^{\rm SA}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>SA</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F^{h,s,r}:=F^{\rm FF}\circ F^{\rm SA},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm SA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>SA</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm SA}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> heads and hidden dimension <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm FF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm FF}</annotation></semantics></math> has hidden dimension <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then we define the transformer networks function class as composition of transformer blocks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Transformer Network Function Class)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let transformer block <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{h,s,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{h,s,r}</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in <a href="#A2.Thmdefinition1" title="Definition B.1 (Transformer Block). ‣ B.1 Transformers ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Background: Transformer Block ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.
Then we define the transformer network function class <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function class with each component being the composition of transformer blocks:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}=\{\tau:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\mid\tau=F^{h,s,r}\circ\cdots\circ F^{h,s,r}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}=\{\tau:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\mid\tau=F^{h,s,r}\circ\cdots\circ F^{h,s,r}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discrete Flow Matching Transformers.</span>
Following the common structure of diffusion transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peebles and Xie, 2023</a>)</cite> and flow matching transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we introduce the transformer architecture used in this paper.
We start with the definition of a reshape layer that converts a vector input <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> into a matrix input <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}=d\times L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}=d\times L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Reshape Layer)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reshape layer <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> is an operator transforming vector input of dimension <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> to matrix output of size <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times L</annotation></semantics></math>.
Te reshape layer is frozen when training.
Further, we define the reverse reshape layer as <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{-1}(\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{-1}(\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For instance, the most commonly used reshape layer in diffusion models is the operator turning vector input of dimension <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> to matrix input of size <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times L</annotation></semantics></math> by rearranging entries, where <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}=d\cdot L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}=d\cdot L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we define the following transformer function class with reshape layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Transformer Function Class With Reshape Layer and Parameter Bound)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm E}(Z):=Z+E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm E}(Z):=Z+E</annotation></semantics></math> represent the position encoding layer and <math id="A2.Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> represent the reshape layer.
The transformer network class with reshape layer is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}_{R}:=\{R^{-1}\circ f_{\mathcal{T}}\circ F^{\rm E}\circ R:\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}\mid f_{\mathcal{T}}\in\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}_{R}:=\{R^{-1}\circ f_{\mathcal{T}}\circ F^{\rm E}\circ R:\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}\mid f_{\mathcal{T}}\in\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="A2.Thmdefinition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{KQ}^{i}:=(W_{K}^{i})^{\top}W_{Q}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{KQ}^{i}:=(W_{K}^{i})^{\top}W_{Q}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmdefinition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{OV}^{i}:=W_{O}^{i}W_{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{OV}^{i}:=W_{O}^{i}W_{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity of notations.
Then, a transformer function class with reshape layer and parameter bound is defined as as <math id="A2.Thmdefinition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}_{R}(C_{\mathcal{T}},C^{2,\infty}_{KQ},C_{KQ},C^{2,\infty}_{OV},C_{OV},C_{E},C^{2,\infty}_{F},C_{F},L_{\mathcal{T}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}_{R}(C_{\mathcal{T}},C^{2,\infty}_{KQ},C_{KQ},C^{2,\infty}_{OV},C_{OV},C_{E},C^{2,\infty}_{F},C_{F},L_{\mathcal{T}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h,s,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h,s,r</annotation></semantics></math> as defined above;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Transformer output bound: <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{Z}\|f_{\mathcal{T}}(Z)\|\leq C_{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>Z</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{Z}\|f_{\mathcal{T}}(Z)\|\leq C_{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parameter bound in <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm FF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm FF}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{\|W_{1}\|_{2,\infty},\|W_{2}\|_{2,\infty}\}\leq C^{2,\infty}_{F},\penalty\ \max\{\|W_{1}\|_{2},\|W_{2}\|_{2}\}\leq C^{2}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{\|W_{1}\|_{2,\infty},\|W_{2}\|_{2,\infty}\}\leq C^{2,\infty}_{F},\penalty\ \max\{\|W_{1}\|_{2},\|W_{2}\|_{2}\}\leq C^{2}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parameter bound in <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm SA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>SA</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm SA}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{KQ}^{i}\|_{2}\leq C_{KQ},\penalty\ \|W_{OV}^{i}\|_{2}\leq C_{OV},\penalty\ \|W_{KQ}^{i}\|_{2,\infty}\leq C^{2,\infty}_{KQ},\penalty\ \|W_{OV}^{i}\|_{2}\leq C^{2,\infty}_{OV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{KQ}^{i}\|_{2}\leq C_{KQ},\penalty\ \|W_{OV}^{i}\|_{2}\leq C_{OV},\penalty\ \|W_{KQ}^{i}\|_{2,\infty}\leq C^{2,\infty}_{KQ},\penalty\ \|W_{OV}^{i}\|_{2}\leq C^{2,\infty}_{OV}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parameter bound in <math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm E}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|E^{\top}\|_{2,\infty}\leq C_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|E^{\top}\|_{2,\infty}\leq C_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Frobenius Lipschitzness of <math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{T}}\in\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{T}}\in\mathcal{T}^{h,s,r}</annotation></semantics></math>:<math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathcal{T}}(Z_{1})-f_{\mathcal{T}}(Z_{2})\|_{F}\leq L_{\mathcal{T}}\|Z_{1}-Z_{2}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathcal{T}}(Z_{1})-f_{\mathcal{T}}(Z_{2})\|_{F}\leq L_{\mathcal{T}}\|Z_{1}-Z_{2}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Lipschitzness of Transformer Network</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prepare our proofs, we first establish a new result on the Lipschitzness of transformer networks (i.e., <a href="#A2.Thmlemma7" title="Lemma B.7 (Lipschitzness of Transformer Block). ‣ Lipschitzness of Transformer. ‣ B.2 Lipschitzness of Transformer Network ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Background: Transformer Block ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>).
It shows that a function composed of Lipschitz functions remains Lipschitz.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Preparations of <a href="#A2.Thmlemma7" title="Lemma B.7 (Lipschitzness of Transformer Block). ‣ Lipschitzness of Transformer. ‣ B.2 Lipschitzness of Transformer Network ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Background: Transformer Block ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first present some helper lemmas for proving <a href="#A2.Thmlemma7" title="Lemma B.7 (Lipschitzness of Transformer Block). ‣ Lipschitzness of Transformer. ‣ B.2 Lipschitzness of Transformer Network ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Background: Transformer Block ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1},f_{2}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1},f_{2}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz w.r.t. Frobenius norm <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.
Then <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}\circ f_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}\circ f_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L_{1}L_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L_{1}L_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f_{1}\circ f_{2}(X_{1})-f_{1}\circ f_{2}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f_{1}\circ f_{2}(X_{1})-f_{1}\circ f_{2}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ L_{2}\|f_{1}(X_{1})-f_{1}(X_{2})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ L_{2}\|f_{1}(X_{1})-f_{1}(X_{2})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ L_{1}L_{2}\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ L_{1}L_{2}\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first line is by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{2}(X_{1})-f_{2}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq L_{2}\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{2}(X_{1})-f_{2}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq L_{2}\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and the second line is by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{1}(X_{1})-f_{1}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq L_{1}\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{1}(X_{1})-f_{1}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq L_{1}\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we analyze the Lipschitzness of RELU function.
Throughout this paper, we treat <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> as element-wise operator when applied to vectors or matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitzness of <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ReLU function <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to the Frobenius norm <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(X_{1})-\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(X_{2})\|_{F}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(X_{1})-\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(X_{2})\|_{F}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{L}|\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}((X_{1})_{i,j})-\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}((X_{2})_{i,j})|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{L}|\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}((X_{1})_{i,j})-\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}((X_{2})_{i,j})|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right"><span id="A2.Ex8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(<span id="A2.Ex8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:67%;">By the definition of Frobenius Norm</span>)</span></span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{L}|(X_{1})_{i,j}-(X_{2})_{i,j}|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{L}|(X_{1})_{i,j}-(X_{2})_{i,j}|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second line is by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(x_{1})-\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(x_{2})|\leq|x_{1}-x_{2}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(x_{1})-\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(x_{2})|\leq|x_{1}-x_{2}|</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">With <a href="#A2.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma B.2 (Lipschitzness of 𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴(⋅)). ‣ Preparations of . ‣ B.2 Lipschitzness of Transformer Network ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Background: Transformer Block ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, we now prove the Lipschitzness of feed-forward layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitzness of FFN)<span id="A2.Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> and define the feedforward layer as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F^{\rm FF}(Z):=Z+W_{2}\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}Z+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})+b_{2}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F^{\rm FF}(Z):=Z+W_{2}\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}Z+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})+b_{2}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm FF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm FF}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous with respect to Frobenius norm, with Lipschitz constant
<math id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{1}\|_{2}\cdot\|W_{2}\|_{2}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{1}\|_{2}\cdot\|W_{2}\|_{2}+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \|F^{\rm FF}(X_{1})-F^{\rm FF}(X_{2})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>FF</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \|F^{\rm FF}(X_{1})-F^{\rm FF}(X_{2})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}+\|(W_{2}\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}X_{1}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})+b_{2}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})-(W_{2}\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}X_{2}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})+b_{2}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}+\|(W_{2}\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}X_{1}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})+b_{2}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})-(W_{2}\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}X_{2}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})+b_{2}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right"><span id="A2.Ex13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(<span id="A2.Ex13.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:67%;">By triangle inequality</span>)</span></span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}+\|W_{2}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}X_{1}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})-\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}X_{2}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}+\|W_{2}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}X_{1}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})-\mathop{\mathsf{ReLU}}(W_{1}X_{2}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}+\|W_{2}\|_{2}\cdot\|(W_{1}X_{1}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})-(W_{1}X_{2}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}+\|W_{2}\|_{2}\cdot\|(W_{1}X_{1}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})-(W_{1}X_{2}+b_{1}\mathds{1}_{L}^{\top})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}+\|W_{1}\|_{2}\cdot\|W_{2}\|_{2}\cdot\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}+\|W_{1}\|_{2}\cdot\|W_{2}\|_{2}\cdot\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ (\|W_{1}\|_{2}\cdot\|W_{2}\|_{2}+1)\cdot\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ (\|W_{1}\|_{2}\cdot\|W_{2}\|_{2}+1)\cdot\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the third line is by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|AX\|_{F}\leq\|A\|_{2}\|X\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|AX\|_{F}\leq\|A\|_{2}\|X\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, the fourth line is by <a href="#A2.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma B.2 (Lipschitzness of 𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴(⋅)). ‣ Preparations of . ‣ B.2 Lipschitzness of Transformer Network ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Background: Transformer Block ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, and the fifth line is by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|AX\|_{F}\leq\|A\|_{2}\|X\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|AX\|_{F}\leq\|A\|_{2}\|X\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we establish the Lipschitzness of self-attention.
We remark that <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Castin et al. (2024)</a></cite> also establish similar results but with a different method not applicable in our setting.
We start with a lemma proving Lipschitzness of any function whose Jacobian norm is uniformly bounded.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitzness of Functions with Bounded Jacobian; Modified from Lemma A.6 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Edelman et al., 2022</a>)</cite>)<span id="A2.Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta^{n-1}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}|x\geq 0,\|x\|_{1}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{n-1}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}|x\geq 0,\|x\|_{1}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-simplex.
Suppose <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\Delta^{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\Delta^{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable and satisfies <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Jf(x)\|_{2}\leq c_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Jf(x)\|_{2}\leq c_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for all <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f(x_{1})-f(x_{2})\|_{2}\leq c_{f}\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f(x_{1})-f(x_{2})\|_{2}\leq c_{f}\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our proof follows the proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Edelman et al., 2022</a>, Lemma A.6)</cite>.
With Newton-Leibniz formula and change of variables, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f(x_{1})-f(x_{2})\|_{2}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f(x_{1})-f(x_{2})\|_{2}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \|(\int_{0}^{1}J(tx_{1}+(1-t)x_{2})\differential t)(x_{1}-x_{2})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \|(\int_{0}^{1}J(tx_{1}+(1-t)x_{2})\differential t)(x_{1}-x_{2})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \int_{0}^{1}\|J(tx_{1}+(1-t)x_{2})(x_{1}-x_{2})\|_{2}\differential t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \int_{0}^{1}\|J(tx_{1}+(1-t)x_{2})(x_{1}-x_{2})\|_{2}\differential t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right"><span id="A2.Ex20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(<span id="A2.Ex20.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:67%;">By Jensen’s inequality</span>)</span></span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \int_{0}^{1}\|J(tx_{1}+(1-t)x_{2})\|_{2}\cdot\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|_{2}\differential t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \int_{0}^{1}\|J(tx_{1}+(1-t)x_{2})\|_{2}\cdot\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|_{2}\differential t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right"><span id="A2.Ex21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(<math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Ax\|_{2}\leq\|A\|_{2}\|x\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Ax\|_{2}\leq\|A\|_{2}\|x\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ c_{f}\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ c_{f}\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right"><span id="A2.Ex22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(<math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Jf(x)\|_{2}\leq c_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" maxsize="0.670em" minsize="0.670em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" mathsize="0.670em">f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Jf(x)\|_{2}\leq c_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">With <a href="#A2.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma B.4 (Lipschitzness of Functions with Bounded Jacobian; Modified from Lemma A.6 of ( , )). ‣ Preparations of . ‣ B.2 Lipschitzness of Transformer Network ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Background: Transformer Block ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we now prove the Lipschitzness of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitzness of <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>; Modified from Corollary A.7 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Edelman et al., 2022</a>)</cite>)<span id="A2.Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the column-wise softmax function.
Then for all <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{1})-\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{1})-\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the simplicity of presentation, let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the (element-wise) softmax function.
Its Jacobian is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=\diag(s)-ss^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=\diag(s)-ss^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric and positive semi-definite, so its singular values equal its eigenvalues.
Recall that for softmax function, its Jacobian matrix’s eigenvalues are smaller than 1.
Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|J\|_{2}\leq 1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|J\|_{2}\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J\|_{2}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J\|_{2}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> with <a href="#A2.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma B.4 (Lipschitzness of Functions with Bounded Jacobian; Modified from Lemma A.6 of ( , )). ‣ Preparations of . ‣ B.2 Lipschitzness of Transformer Network ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Background: Transformer Block ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, for each column <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{1})-\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{2}))_{\cdot,i}\|_{2}\leq\|(X_{1}-X_{2})_{\cdot,i}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{1})-\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{2}))_{\cdot,i}\|_{2}\leq\|(X_{1}-X_{2})_{\cdot,i}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over all columns gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{1})-\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{1})-\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}(X_{2})\|_{F}\leq\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we prove the Lipschitzness of self-attention layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitzness of Multi-Head Self-Attention)<span id="A2.Thmlemma6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X\|_{2}\leq B_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X\|_{2}\leq B_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> on a compact domain.
Define <math id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm SA}(X):=X+\sum_{i=1}^{h}W_{O}^{i}(W_{V}^{i}X)\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}((W_{K}^{i}X)^{\top}(W_{Q}^{i}X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>SA</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">Softmax</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm SA}(X):=X+\sum_{i=1}^{h}W_{O}^{i}(W_{V}^{i}X)\mathop{{\rm Softmax}}((W_{K}^{i}X)^{\top}(W_{Q}^{i}X))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm SA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>SA</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm SA}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous w.r.t. the Frobenius norm <math id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, with Lipschitz constant</p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1+2(B_{X})^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{h}\|W^{i}_{OV}\|_{2}\cdot\|W^{i}_{KQ}\|_{2}+L\sum_{i=1}^{h}\|W^{i}_{OV}\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1+2(B_{X})^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{h}\|W^{i}_{OV}\|_{2}\cdot\|W^{i}_{KQ}\|_{2}+L\sum_{i=1}^{h}\|W^{i}_{OV}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{i}_{OV}=W_{O}^{i}W_{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{i}_{OV}=W_{O}^{i}W_{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{i}_{KQ}=(W_{K}^{i})^{\top}W_{Q}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{i}_{KQ}=(W_{K}^{i})^{\top}W_{Q}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.Thmlemma6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[h]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">For every <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X_{1}\|_{2},\|X_{2}\|_{2}\leq B_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X_{1}\|_{2},\|X_{2}\|_{2}\leq B_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
